{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["But now he first explains why the Egyptians would say thus — for they heard that You brought them out with great might, with the pillar of fire and the pillar of cloud, all in the manner of exceeding love and fondness. And in the end You slaughter them like one man?! And the Egyptians will say: not out of hatred did He do so to them, but out of inability to fight against thirty-one kings. And now, turn back from Your fierce wrath — for the sake of Your name, that it not be profaned."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "The subject shifts between speakers without explicit markers: 'he first explains' is Moshe addressing Elohim in prayer; the questions and the report of what Egypt will say are Moshe's words to Elohim; 'turn back from Your fierce wrath' is Moshe's plea."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:50:12.664001650Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}